### Test 1: Book without logging in (Expect 401 Unauthorized)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/customer/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 1
}

### Test 2: Login as Customer (Establishes HttpSession)
# @name customerLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sjsustudentA",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Test 3: Book slot 1 with a valid customer session (Expect 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/customer/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 1
}

### Test 3b: Book the same slot again (Expect 409 Conflict, double-booking guard)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/customer/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 1
}

### Test 4: Customer cancels the appointment (Expect 200 OK)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/customer/appointments/1

### Test 5: Customer attempts a provider action (Expect 403 Forbidden)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/provider/slots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "startTime": "2026-12-10T10:00:00",
  "endTime": "2026-12-10T11:00:00"
}

### Test 6: Login as Provider (Overrides the HttpSession)
# @name providerLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sjsuTutorA",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Test 7: Provider creates a future slot (Expect 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/provider/slots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "startTime": "2026-12-10T10:00:00",
  "endTime": "2026-12-10T11:00:00"
}

### Test 8: Provider views their slots (Expect 200 OK with list)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/provider/slots

### Test 9: Provider creates a past slot (Expect 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/provider/slots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "startTime": "2020-01-01T10:00:00",
  "endTime": "2020-01-01T11:00:00"
}

### Test 10: Provider tries to book (Expect 403 Forbidden)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/customer/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slotId": 1
}

### Test 11: Register a new provider (Expect 201 Created, the SQL fix)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newtutor",
  "password": "pass123",
  "role": "PROVIDER",
  "displayName": "New Tutor"
}

### Test 12: Browse available slots, no login needed (Expect 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/slots

### Test 13: Who am I (Expect 200 OK with the provider's info)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Test 14: Logout
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout



